---
system: sys-13-security-secrets-management
flow_id: cert-verification-and-revocation
surface: internal-RPC
spec_anchor: /software/systems/13-security-secrets-management#certificate-verification
actors: [Device, RealtimeService, CertificateVerifier, Redis, PostgreSQL, AdminConsole, DeviceService]
apis:
  - GET /v1/realtime/connect
externals: []
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - cert_revoked_redis_hit
  - cert_not_in_postgres
  - cert_device_id_mismatch
  - cert_expired
  - cert_status_provisioned_to_active_failure
idempotency: status transition provisioned→active is one-shot on first successful handshake; revocation idempotent (status='revoked' is terminal)
retry: device retries on TLS reject only after factory-reset (rerun manufacturing)
timeout: 50ms p99 cert verification (5ms Redis fast-path)
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Device
    participant RealtimeService
    participant CertificateVerifier
    participant Redis
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant AdminConsole
    participant DeviceService

    Device->>RealtimeService: TLS ClientHello and certificate (mTLS)
    RealtimeService->>CertificateVerifier: verify(cert)
    CertificateVerifier->>Redis: SISMEMBER revoked_certs cert_fingerprint
    alt cert_revoked_redis_hit
        Redis-->>CertificateVerifier: 1 (revoked)
        CertificateVerifier-->>RealtimeService: REJECT
        RealtimeService--xDevice: TLS handshake fails
    else not_in_revoked_set
        Redis-->>CertificateVerifier: 0
        CertificateVerifier->>PostgreSQL: SELECT * FROM device_certificates WHERE certificate_fingerprint=$1 AND device_id=$2
        alt cert_not_in_postgres
            PostgreSQL-->>CertificateVerifier: 0 rows
            CertificateVerifier-->>RealtimeService: REJECT
        else cert_device_id_mismatch
            PostgreSQL-->>CertificateVerifier: row with different device_id
            CertificateVerifier-->>RealtimeService: REJECT
        else cert_expired
            PostgreSQL-->>CertificateVerifier: expires_at < now()
            CertificateVerifier-->>RealtimeService: REJECT
        else first_handshake (status='provisioned')
            PostgreSQL-->>CertificateVerifier: status='provisioned'
            CertificateVerifier->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE device_certificates SET status='active', first_seen_at=now()
            alt cert_status_provisioned_to_active_failure
                PostgreSQL--xCertificateVerifier: deadlock or unique violation
                CertificateVerifier-->>RealtimeService: REJECT, emit security event
            else success
                CertificateVerifier-->>RealtimeService: ALLOW
            end
        else status_active
            CertificateVerifier-->>RealtimeService: ALLOW
        end
    end

    Note over AdminConsole,DeviceService: Revocation trigger — admin action, device anomaly, automated detection (CertAnomalyDetector)
    AdminConsole->>DeviceService: POST /admin/devices/:deviceId/revoke-cert {reason}
    DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE device_certificates SET status='revoked', revoked_at=now(), revoked_by, revocation_reason
    DeviceService->>Redis: SADD revoked_certs cert_fingerprint
    DeviceService->>Redis: PUBLISH device_disconnect {device_id} (sys-04 orchestrator terminates active WS)
    DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT security_events {event_type='cert_revoked', severity='warning'}
    DeviceService-->>AdminConsole: 204

    Note over Device: next connection attempt receives TLS reject → enters local-only mode until factory-reset and re-provision

    Note over Device,PostgreSQL: verification p99 <50ms · Redis fast-path <5ms · revocation propagation via Redis pub/sub and revoked_certs set
